# Lint configuration for hft_engine.
#
# This enables the bug-finding families and leaves the style families off.
# clang-format already owns style, and turning on modernize-*/readability-*
# wholesale produced ~700 findings that were almost entirely cosmetic — a gate
# that large gets disabled rather than fixed.
#
# Every exclusion below is a check that fires on this codebase for a reason
# that is deliberate, so each one names its justification. The intent is that
# this list stays short and auditable, and that the set is tightened as the
# cosmetic families are worked through.
Checks: >
  clang-analyzer-*,
  bugprone-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-exception-escape,
  -bugprone-throwing-static-initialization,
  -bugprone-random-generator-seed

# Why each exclusion:
#
#   clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding
#     Reports 206 padding bytes in Engine and 188 in FeedHandler and suggests
#     a "optimal" field order. That padding is `alignas(kCacheLineSize)` on the
#     SPSC producer/consumer cursors and the feed buffer, which exists
#     specifically to keep them on separate cache lines. Taking the analyzer's
#     advice would compact the struct and reintroduce the false sharing the
#     design is built to avoid.
#
#   portability-avoid-pragma-once
#     The tree uses `#pragma once` in all 19 headers. Every toolchain in the CI
#     matrix supports it; converting to include guards would be churn for no
#     portability gain.
#
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#     Fires on numeric constructors like (price, size) and (num, den). Real in
#     principle, but the fix is a strong-typedef refactor of the wire structs,
#     which is out of proportion to the risk in a codebase this size.
#
#   bugprone-exception-escape
#   bugprone-throwing-static-initialization
#     Both fire only on the test and benchmark drivers: `main` in each driver,
#     and the static `Registrar` objects that the HFT_TEST macro declares to
#     self-register cases. Neither is engine code and neither is on the hot
#     path. No noexcept function in include/hft/ triggers either check.
#
#   bugprone-random-generator-seed
#     Fires on the constant seeds in test_book, test_itch and test_histogram.
#     Those seeds are deliberate: the figure and test pipeline is required to
#     be deterministic, so a fixed seed is the correct choice and a
#     nondeterministic one would be the defect.

WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: 'include/hft/.*\.hpp$'
FormatStyle: file
